<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 40,983 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 40,983 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 40,983 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 62,466 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   March 18</p>
<p>    Export cargo		17,579	14,404</p>
<p>    Import cargo		23,404	48,062</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, eight ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, six are expected to sail and six are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Ying Song Hu	 19/3</p>
<p>Containers		  240	 Dammam Bay	   19/3</p>
<p>Phosphate		29,887	 Lapanto Glory	20/3</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 40,000	 Miraj		  20/3</p>
<p>Gas/kerosene oil     56,000	 Warbah		 22/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
